IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Notaries Public Act 1959 (Singapore) -- whether I can be appointed a notary public, permanently (s 3(1)-(4)) or temporarily
-- in place of an absent notary (s 3(5)); whether I am a notary public on a given day (s 2, s 3(1), (6), ss 5, 6); what I may do
-- with an affidavit or statutory declaration (s 4(2), (3)); whether my appointment must or may be revoked (ss 5, 6); and whether
-- I commit an offence by acting as a notary public, and the most I can be fined (s 7).
--
-- SEAT: the advocate and solicitor who is, or wants to be, a notary public in Singapore -- and, for s 7, anyone who exercises a
-- notary's functions in Singapore. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it. The Senate of the Singapore Academy
-- of Law appoints and revokes; what it may or must do is encoded as what it means for that person.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 2 ("notary public"), s 3(1)-(6), s 4(2) and (3)(a)-(b), s 5(a)-(c), s 6, s 7.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December
-- 2021), SSO "Current version as at 05 Oct 2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NPA1959.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the long title and s 1, which decide nothing; s 3(7) (Gazette publication of appointments and lapses), to which
-- the Act attaches no consequence; s 8 (rule-making by the Chief Justice), which is machinery. The Notaries Public Rules made
-- under s 8 are NOT deposited, so the fees they fix and any powers they prescribe under s 4(3)(c) are not encoded; nor are "the
-- powers and functions which are ordinarily exercised by notaries public in England" (s 4(1)), which the Act borrows and does
-- not state. Where an answer turns on either, the decision says `not covered by this encoding`.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Notaries Public Act 1959`

§§ `3. Appointment of notaries public -- what I can state about myself`

-- s 3(1): "The Senate may, from time to time, appoint fit and proper persons to be notaries public for a period not exceeding
-- 12 months."
-- s 3(2): "No person shall be appointed as a notary public unless he is a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore and has
-- so practised for not less than 7 years."
-- s 3(3): "The Senate shall not make any appointment under this section without consulting the Council of the Law Society of
-- Singapore".
-- s 3(5): "If it appears to the Senate that any notary public is about to be absent from Singapore for a period exceeding one
-- month, the Senate may appoint any person, being a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore, to be a notary public
-- temporarily during the absence of that notary public from Singapore."
--
-- "Senate": the Senate of the Singapore Academy of Law (s 2). "Practising advocate and solicitor" is a term borrowed from the
-- Legal Profession Act 1966, so it is asked as a fact. Whether I am "fit and proper", and whether a notary "appears" to the
-- Senate to be about to be absent, are the Senate's judgments: they are inputs, and answers that turn on them say so.
DECLARE `Me as a candidate` HAS
    `I am a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(2), (5): a borrowed term, asked
    `the years I have practised as an advocate and solicitor in Singapore` IS A NUMBER  -- s 3(2): "so practised"
    `the Senate finds me a fit and proper person`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(1): the Senate's judgment
    `the Senate has consulted the Council of the Law Society`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(3): the Council of the Law Society of
                                                                                  -- Singapore, under the Legal Profession Act 1966
    `the period sought in months`                                  IS A NUMBER    -- s 3(1), (6): "not exceeding 12 months"
    `it appears to the Senate that the notary I would stand in for is about to be absent from Singapore for more than one month`
                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(5): the Senate's judgment

-- The answers s 3 gives me, in its own terms.
DECLARE `What section 3 says about appointing me` IS ONE OF
    `yes, if the Senate chooses: it has absolute discretion and there is no appeal from its decision`
    `no: section 3(2) requires a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
    `no: section 3(2) requires not less than 7 years in practice`
    `no: section 3(1) appoints only persons the Senate finds fit and proper`
    `not until the Senate has consulted the Council of the Law Society, as section 3(3) requires`
    `no: an appointment may not be for more than 12 months`
    `no: section 3(5) requires a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
    `no: section 3(5) applies only while a notary public is about to be absent from Singapore for more than one month`

§§ `3(2). Am I eligible to be appointed`

-- s 3(2): "not less than 7 years": 7 years is enough.
GIVEN me IS A `Me as a candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible to be appointed a notary public` me IF
        me's `I am a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
    ... me's `the years I have practised as an advocate and solicitor in Singapore` AT LEAST 7

§§ `3(1)-(4). Can I be appointed a notary public`

-- s 3(4): "In making any appointment under this section, the Senate shall have regard to the number of notaries public already
-- practising in the place where the applicant proposes to practise and to the convenience of the inhabitants of that place,
-- but, subject to this, the Senate shall have absolute discretion in making or refusing to make any such appointment and there
-- shall be no appeal from its decision."
-- The number of notaries in my place and the convenience of its inhabitants are what the Senate must weigh; they are not a
-- condition I can meet or fail. So when every condition is met, the answer is only that the Senate MAY appoint me.
GIVEN me IS A `Me as a candidate`
GIVETH A `What section 3 says about appointing me`
DECIDE `Can I be appointed a notary public` me IS
    BRANCH
      IF NOT me's `I am a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
        THEN `no: section 3(2) requires a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
      IF me's `the years I have practised as an advocate and solicitor in Singapore` LESS THAN 7
        THEN `no: section 3(2) requires not less than 7 years in practice`
      IF me's `the period sought in months` GREATER THAN 12
        THEN `no: an appointment may not be for more than 12 months`
      IF NOT me's `the Senate finds me a fit and proper person`
        THEN `no: section 3(1) appoints only persons the Senate finds fit and proper`
      IF NOT me's `the Senate has consulted the Council of the Law Society`
        THEN `not until the Senate has consulted the Council of the Law Society, as section 3(3) requires`
      OTHERWISE `yes, if the Senate chooses: it has absolute discretion and there is no appeal from its decision`

-- s 3(4): "there shall be no appeal from its decision" -- whether the Senate appoints me or refuses.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I appeal against the Senate's decision on my appointment` IF FALSE

§§ `3(5), (6). Can I be appointed temporarily in place of an absent notary`

-- s 3(5) asks only that I be "a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore". It does not repeat the 7 years of s 3(2) or
-- the "fit and proper" of s 3(1). READING TAKEN: s 3(2) ("No person shall be appointed as a notary public unless ...") is read
-- as governing appointments under s 3(1) only, because s 3(5) states its own qualification; on the other reading a temporary
-- appointee would need 7 years too. The words of s 3(3) and (4) ("any appointment under this section") reach a temporary
-- appointment: the Council must be consulted, and the Senate's discretion is absolute.
-- s 3(6): "No temporary appointment of a notary public shall have effect for a period longer than 12 months".
GIVEN me IS A `Me as a candidate`
GIVETH A `What section 3 says about appointing me`
DECIDE `Can I be appointed a notary public temporarily` me IS
    BRANCH
      IF NOT me's `it appears to the Senate that the notary I would stand in for is about to be absent from Singapore for more than one month`
        THEN `no: section 3(5) applies only while a notary public is about to be absent from Singapore for more than one month`
      IF NOT me's `I am a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
        THEN `no: section 3(5) requires a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
      IF me's `the period sought in months` GREATER THAN 12
        THEN `no: an appointment may not be for more than 12 months`
      IF NOT me's `the Senate has consulted the Council of the Law Society`
        THEN `not until the Senate has consulted the Council of the Law Society, as section 3(3) requires`
      OTHERWISE `yes, if the Senate chooses: it has absolute discretion and there is no appeal from its decision`

§§ `2, 3(1), 3(6), 5, 6. Am I a notary public on a given day`

-- s 2: "notary public" means "a person who has been appointed as a notary public under section 3 but does not include any
-- person whose appointment has been revoked under section 5".
-- s 3(1): "for a period not exceeding 12 months".
-- s 3(6): a temporary appointment has no effect "for a period longer than 12 months" and "shall lapse on the death or on the
-- return to Singapore of the notary public on account of whose departure from Singapore the appointment was made".
-- s 5: "the Senate shall by order revoke the appointment". s 6: "the Senate may, by notification in the Gazette, revoke the
-- appointment".
DECLARE `Kind of appointment` IS ONE OF
    `an appointment under section 3(1)`
    `a temporary appointment under section 3(5)`

-- The facts I can state about my appointment.
DECLARE `My appointment` HAS
    `the kind`                                    IS A `Kind of appointment`
    `it took effect on`                           IS A DATE
    `the period stated in months`                 IS A NUMBER
    `it was revoked by order under section 5 on`  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `it was revoked at my request under section 6 on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the absent notary returned to Singapore on`  IS A MAYBE DATE   -- s 3(6): read only for a temporary appointment
    `the absent notary died on`                   IS A MAYBE DATE   -- s 3(6): read only for a temporary appointment

DECLARE `My standing as a notary public` IS ONE OF
    `I am a notary public`
    `not yet: my appointment has not taken effect`
    `no: the period of my appointment has run out`
    `no: my appointment was revoked under section 5, and section 2 excludes me`
    `no: my appointment was revoked at my request under section 6`
    `no: my temporary appointment lapsed on the return to Singapore of the absent notary`
    `no: my temporary appointment lapsed on the death of the absent notary`
    `not covered by this encoding: an appointment stated for more than 12 months, which section 3 does not allow`

-- An event that may have happened, and whether it had happened by the day asked about. READING TAKEN: a revocation or a lapse
-- operates from the day it happens, so on that day I am no longer a notary public.
GIVEN `the event` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `had it happened by` `the event` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `the date` THEN `the date` AT MOST `the day`

-- READING TAKEN on counting the period (an inference, not in the text): an appointment for N months runs from the day it took
-- effect to the day before the same date N months on, so a 12-month appointment from 1 January 2026 is in effect on 31 December
-- 2026 and not on 1 January 2027. A day that does not exist in the end month is clamped to the month's last day.
GIVEN a IS A `My appointment`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day my appointment's period runs out` a MEANS
    `add months` (a's `it took effect on`) (a's `the period stated in months`)

-- s 2 excludes only a person whose appointment was revoked under s 5. READING TAKEN: a revocation under s 6 also ends my
-- standing, because s 6 revokes "the appointment" in the same words as s 5, and I am then no longer a person holding an
-- appointment under s 3. The text does not say so in terms.
GIVEN a IS A `My appointment`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `My standing as a notary public`
DECIDE `Am I a notary public` a `the day` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `the day` LESS THAN a's `it took effect on`
        THEN `not yet: my appointment has not taken effect`
      IF a's `the period stated in months` GREATER THAN 12
        THEN `not covered by this encoding: an appointment stated for more than 12 months, which section 3 does not allow`
      IF `had it happened by` (a's `it was revoked by order under section 5 on`) `the day`
        THEN `no: my appointment was revoked under section 5, and section 2 excludes me`
      IF `had it happened by` (a's `it was revoked at my request under section 6 on`) `the day`
        THEN `no: my appointment was revoked at my request under section 6`
      IF a's `the kind` EQUALS `a temporary appointment under section 3(5)`
         AND `had it happened by` (a's `the absent notary died on`) `the day`
        THEN `no: my temporary appointment lapsed on the death of the absent notary`
      IF a's `the kind` EQUALS `a temporary appointment under section 3(5)`
         AND `had it happened by` (a's `the absent notary returned to Singapore on`) `the day`
        THEN `no: my temporary appointment lapsed on the return to Singapore of the absent notary`
      IF `the day` AT LEAST `the day my appointment's period runs out` a
        THEN `no: the period of my appointment has run out`
      OTHERWISE `I am a notary public`

GIVEN a IS A `My appointment`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `am I a notary public on the day` a `the day` IF
    `Am I a notary public` a `the day` EQUALS `I am a notary public`

§§ `4. Privileges of notaries public -- affidavits and statutory declarations`

-- s 4(1): "Every notary public shall have and may exercise within Singapore all the powers and functions which are ordinarily
-- exercised by notaries public in England." -- borrowed, not stated; NOT encoded.
-- s 4(2): "Except for the purposes of and to the extent necessary to give effect to subsection (3), powers under subsection (1)
-- shall not include power to administer any oath or affirmation in connection with any affidavit or statutory declaration which
-- is executed for the purpose of being used in any court or place within Singapore or to take or attest any such affidavit or
-- statutory declaration."
-- s 4(3): "a notary public may -- (a) administer any oath or affirmation in connection with any affidavit or statutory
-- declaration which is executed -- (i) for the purpose of confirming or proving the due execution of any document; (ii) by any
-- master or member of the crew of any vessel in respect of any matter concerning the vessel; or (iii) for the purpose of being
-- used in any court or place outside Singapore; (b) take or attest any affidavit or statutory declaration referred to in
-- paragraph (a); and (c) have and exercise such other powers and functions as may be prescribed."
DECLARE `What the affidavit is about` IS ONE OF
    `confirming or proving the due execution of a document`               -- s 4(3)(a)(i)
    `a matter concerning a vessel, sworn by its master or a crew member`  -- s 4(3)(a)(ii)
    `something else`

-- One affidavit or statutory declaration I am asked to deal with.
DECLARE `The affidavit` HAS
    `what it is about`                                 IS A `What the affidavit is about`
    `it is to be used in a court or place within Singapore`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 4(2)
    `it is to be used in a court or place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 4(3)(a)(iii)

DECLARE `My power over the affidavit` IS ONE OF
    `yes, under section 4(3)(a)(i): it confirms or proves the due execution of a document`
    `yes, under section 4(3)(a)(ii): it is sworn by a vessel's master or crew member about the vessel`
    `yes, under section 4(3)(a)(iii): it is to be used in a court or place outside Singapore`
    `no: section 4(2) takes it out of my powers, because it is to be used in a court or place within Singapore`
    `not covered by this encoding: it turns on English notarial practice (section 4(1)) or prescribed powers (section 4(3)(c))`

-- s 4(2) gives way to s 4(3) ("Except for the purposes of ... subsection (3)"), so the three limbs of s 4(3)(a) are tried
-- first: an affidavit proving due execution, or a crew member's, may be sworn before me even for use in Singapore. The same
-- answer governs administering the oath (s 4(3)(a)) and taking or attesting the affidavit (s 4(3)(b)).
GIVEN aff IS A `The affidavit`
GIVETH A `My power over the affidavit`
DECIDE `May I administer the oath for, take or attest the affidavit` aff IS
    BRANCH
      IF aff's `what it is about` EQUALS `confirming or proving the due execution of a document`
        THEN `yes, under section 4(3)(a)(i): it confirms or proves the due execution of a document`
      IF aff's `what it is about` EQUALS `a matter concerning a vessel, sworn by its master or a crew member`
        THEN `yes, under section 4(3)(a)(ii): it is sworn by a vessel's master or crew member about the vessel`
      IF aff's `it is to be used in a court or place outside Singapore`
        THEN `yes, under section 4(3)(a)(iii): it is to be used in a court or place outside Singapore`
      IF aff's `it is to be used in a court or place within Singapore`
        THEN `no: section 4(2) takes it out of my powers, because it is to be used in a court or place within Singapore`
      OTHERWISE `not covered by this encoding: it turns on English notarial practice (section 4(1)) or prescribed powers (section 4(3)(c))`

§§ `5. Misconduct of notaries public -- must my appointment be revoked`

-- s 5: "If it appears to the Senate that any person being a notary public -- (a) has become a bankrupt or has made an
-- arrangement with his creditors; (b) has been struck off the roll of advocates and solicitors of Singapore; or (c) has been
-- found to be guilty of such professional or other misconduct as, in the opinion of the Senate, renders him unfit to practise
-- as a notary public, the Senate shall by order revoke the appointment of the person and shall cause the order to be published
-- in the Gazette."
-- "Bankrupt", "arrangement with creditors" and "struck off the roll" are borrowed terms, asked as facts. Whether misconduct
-- renders me unfit is "in the opinion of the Senate": an input.
DECLARE `What has happened to me` HAS
    `I have become a bankrupt`                                          IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(a)
    `I have made an arrangement with my creditors`                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(a)
    `I have been struck off the roll of advocates and solicitors of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(b)
    `I have been found guilty of professional or other misconduct`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(c)
    `the Senate is of the opinion that the misconduct renders me unfit to practise as a notary public` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(c)
    `I have stopped practising as an advocate and solicitor`            IS A BOOLEAN   -- not a ground in s 5; read by no rule

DECLARE `What section 5 says about my appointment` IS ONE OF
    `it must be revoked under section 5(a), if it so appears to the Senate, by order published in the Gazette`
    `it must be revoked under section 5(b), if it so appears to the Senate, by order published in the Gazette`
    `it must be revoked under section 5(c), by order published in the Gazette`
    `section 5 does not require it to be revoked`

-- "shall ... revoke": once a ground appears to the Senate, revocation is mandatory. The (c) answer needs no "if" because the
-- Senate's opinion is already an input.
GIVEN h IS A `What has happened to me`
GIVETH A `What section 5 says about my appointment`
DECIDE `Must my appointment be revoked` h IS
    BRANCH
      IF h's `I have become a bankrupt` OR h's `I have made an arrangement with my creditors`
        THEN `it must be revoked under section 5(a), if it so appears to the Senate, by order published in the Gazette`
      IF h's `I have been struck off the roll of advocates and solicitors of Singapore`
        THEN `it must be revoked under section 5(b), if it so appears to the Senate, by order published in the Gazette`
      IF h's `I have been found guilty of professional or other misconduct`
         AND h's `the Senate is of the opinion that the misconduct renders me unfit to practise as a notary public`
        THEN `it must be revoked under section 5(c), by order published in the Gazette`
      OTHERWISE `section 5 does not require it to be revoked`

§§ `6. Revocation at my own request`

-- s 6: "The Senate may, by notification in the Gazette, revoke the appointment of a notary public if the notary public requests
-- that his appointment be revoked." -- "may": the Senate is not bound to.
DECLARE `What section 6 says about my request` IS ONE OF
    `the Senate may revoke my appointment by notification in the Gazette, but need not`
    `section 6 does not apply unless I request revocation`

GIVEN `I have requested that my appointment be revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What section 6 says about my request`
DECIDE `Can I have my appointment revoked at my own request` `I have requested that my appointment be revoked` IS
    IF `I have requested that my appointment be revoked`
    THEN `the Senate may revoke my appointment by notification in the Gazette, but need not`
    ELSE `section 6 does not apply unless I request revocation`

§§ `7. Penalty for exercise of functions of notary public by unauthorised persons`

-- s 7: "Any person who exercises within Singapore any of the functions of a notary public otherwise than in accordance with the
-- provisions of this Act shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction before a District Judge to a fine not
-- exceeding $10,000." [20/2007]
--
-- READING TAKEN: "otherwise than in accordance with the provisions of this Act" is read as covering two cases the Act states:
-- acting when I am not a notary public that day (ss 2, 3, 5, 6), and acting beyond the powers s 4 gives. Breach of rules made
-- under s 8 might also be "otherwise than in accordance with" the Act; the rules are not deposited and that case is not encoded.
DECLARE `The notarial act` IS ONE OF
    `administering an oath for, taking or attesting an affidavit or statutory declaration` HAS
        `the affidavit concerned` IS A `The affidavit`
    `another function of a notary public`   -- protests, certificates and the like: the Act leaves them to s 4(1)

DECLARE `What section 7 says about my act` IS ONE OF
    `no offence under section 7: the act was not done within Singapore`
    `no offence under section 7: I am a notary public acting within section 4`
    `an offence under section 7: I am not a notary public on that day`
    `an offence under section 7: section 4(2) puts the act outside my powers`
    `not covered by this encoding: whether the act is within my powers turns on English practice or prescribed powers`

GIVEN `the act` IS A `The notarial act`
      `I did it within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was then a notary public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What section 7 says about my act`
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence under section 7` `the act` `I did it within Singapore` `I was then a notary public` IS
    IF NOT `I did it within Singapore`
    THEN `no offence under section 7: the act was not done within Singapore`
    ELSE IF NOT `I was then a notary public`
         THEN `an offence under section 7: I am not a notary public on that day`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the act`
              WHEN `administering an oath for, taking or attesting an affidavit or statutory declaration` aff THEN
                  CONSIDER `May I administer the oath for, take or attest the affidavit` aff
                  WHEN `no: section 4(2) takes it out of my powers, because it is to be used in a court or place within Singapore`
                      THEN `an offence under section 7: section 4(2) puts the act outside my powers`
                  WHEN `not covered by this encoding: it turns on English notarial practice (section 4(1)) or prescribed powers (section 4(3)(c))`
                      THEN `not covered by this encoding: whether the act is within my powers turns on English practice or prescribed powers`
                  OTHERWISE `no offence under section 7: I am a notary public acting within section 4`
              WHEN `another function of a notary public` THEN
                  `not covered by this encoding: whether the act is within my powers turns on English practice or prescribed powers`

-- The same question asked with my appointment and the day, so that ss 2, 3, 5 and 6 decide whether I was a notary public.
-- NOTHING for the appointment means I have never been appointed.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The notarial act`
      `I did it within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my appointment` IS A MAYBE `My appointment`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What section 7 says about my act`
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence under section 7 on the day` `the act` `I did it within Singapore` `my appointment` `the day` IS
    `Do I commit an offence under section 7` `the act` `I did it within Singapore` `was I a notary public`
    WHERE
        `was I a notary public` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my appointment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST a THEN `am I a notary public on the day` a `the day`

-- s 7: "a fine not exceeding $10,000", "on conviction before a District Judge". The Act provides no imprisonment.
`What is the most I can be fined under section 7` MEANS 10000

`Who can convict me under section 7` MEANS "a District Judge"
